{"cross_mech":[],"family":{"alphafold_models":2258,"candidate_reasons":["pfam_previous_unknown_name"],"characterization_status":"","context_evidence_count":null,"cross_mech":{"example_proteins":0,"protein_traits_record":false,"records_by_mech":{},"scanned":false},"curation_status":"SEEDED","demotion_reasons":[],"description":"This entry represents the C-terminal domain of aspartate dehydrogenases that belong to a unique class of amino acid dehydrogenases. The structure of Thermotoga maritima TM1643 has been found to contain an N-terminal Rossmann fold domain (which binds the NAD(P)+ cofactor) and a C-terminal alpha/beta domain [[cite:PUB00014412]]. Enzymatic characterisation of TM1643 revealed that it possesses NAD or NADP-dependent dehydrogenase activity toward L-aspartate but no aspartate oxidase activity [[cite:PUB00014412]]. Members of this group share some structural similarity to several other NAD(P)+-dependent oxidoreductases, including inositol 1-phosphate synthase, dihydrodipicolinate reductase, and ASA-DH [[cite:PUB00014412]]. It has been proposed that in Thermotoga maritima, TM1643 catalyses the first reaction of de novo biosynthesis of NAD from aspartate, and it produces iminoaspartate required for this pathway.","domain_architectures":31,"interpro_id":"IPR002811","known_evidence_count":null,"matches":3195,"name":"Aspartate dehydrogenase, C-terminal","partial_evidence_count":null,"pfam_id":"PF01958","proteins":3184,"proteomes":2698,"short_name":"Asp_DH_C","source_url":"https://www.ebi.ac.uk/interpro/api/entry/pfam/PF01958","structures":3,"taxa":5585,"unknown_status":"EX_DUF"},"inputs":{"cross_mech":"cross-mech-duf-examples-2026-10-10","members":"pfam-uniprot-uniref90-2026-10-07","protein_examples":"duf-protein-examples-2026-10-13","worklist":"interpro-pfam-duf-2026-10-10"},"members":[],"metadata":{"curation_status":"SEEDED","local_source":"source/data/families/PF01958.yaml","record":{"characterization_status":"UNSCORED","counters":{"alphafold_models":225